# Kept out of the deployment: none of it is imported at runtime, so shipping it only grows
# the bundle and widens what the static handler can serve. The root is deployed as-is (see
# README), and the `/:path*` -> `/frontend/:path*` rewrite runs AFTER the filesystem check,
# so any real file at a requested path is served verbatim.
#
# backend/ is deliberately NOT listed. Every api/*.py function does `from app import ...`,
# resolved through api/index.py's sys.path insert into backend/ — excluding it would 404 the
# entire API. Because it ships, everything inside it is potentially fetchable, so the .env
# rules below are not redundant with .gitignore: .gitignore governs what reaches a
# git-connected deploy, THIS file governs `vercel --prod` from a working tree, and the CLI's
# own defaults cover .env.local / .env.*.local but not a plain .env. README tells every
# developer to create backend/.env, and it holds BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN — read/write/delete
# on the whole blob store, across every session. Never let it ship.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
backend/data/

tests/
docs/
test_blots/
test-blots/

venv/
.venv/
backend/venv/
backend/test_security.py

__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Rebuilt by the install step from package.json + package-lock.json, which DO ship — the
# @vercel/blob import in api/blob-upload.js resolves from that install, not from an upload.
node_modules/

# Written by `vercel link` / the first CLI deploy. Holds projectId and orgId; no reason for
# it to make the round trip back up.
.vercel/

# macOS writes these into every directory it browses, and each one lists the directory's
# contents — including names of files since deleted. Three exist in this tree today.
.DS_Store
**/.DS_Store

# Local-only data and scratch output, all gitignored, none of it runtime input.
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
*.log
logs/

.pre-commit-config.yaml
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
